Chapter: ProbeTyvarLeak
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 An unsubstituted type variable reaches the emitted zig as a bare identifier,
 not as a marker.

 `emit-zig-type` renders `is TypeVar (id) -> "T" & integer-to-text id`
 (ZigEmitter.codex:274). Inside a generic body that is right -- the name is a
 `comptime T181: type` parameter and is in scope. At a call site where
 substitution should already have happened and did not, the same rule emits
 `T181` into a scope that has no such name, and zig answers

     error: use of undeclared identifier 'T181'

 which names nothing about Codex, points at a 9,000-column generated line, and
 above all is NOT a `@compileError` marker.

 That last part is the finding rather than the error. Every other unmapped
 construct in this emitter refuses loudly and by name, and two mechanisms
 depend on it: `zig-is-unmapped` tests for the marker to decide whether a
 definition's return type is recoverable, and `corpus_run.py --transpile`
 histograms the markers to rank WHICH GAP TO FIX FIRST. A construct that
 renders as a plausible identifier instead is invisible to both. It does not
 appear in the census ranking at all, so however often it bites, the number
 that decides priorities reads zero.

 Found 2026-08-21 by tier 8 -- `__linked-list-empty` in a statement position,
 where nothing supplies an expected type. The same call with a type context
 emits `cx_ll_with_capacity(i64, 4)` and compiles, which is why eleven days of
 rung sweeps never met it: every real use in the compiler has a context.

 Both lines below are the SAME BUILTIN. The first has a return type to be read
 from and works. The second does not and leaks. Run it through `codexir` and
 `zigemit` and grep the emitted zig for `T` followed by digits; the failure is
 visible without compiling, which is the point -- a marker would have been.

Section: Shapes

 Context supplied by the signature. This one is fine.

  typed-empty : Integer -> List Integer
  typed-empty (n) = __linked-list-empty n

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni "-- with a type context, the element type is read from the signature --"
   print-line-uni ("typed empty has length 0   : " & (if list-length (typed-empty 4) == 0 then "yes" else "no"))
   print-line-uni "-- without one, the type variable is emitted verbatim --"
   print-line-uni ("untyped empty has length 0 : " & (if list-length (__linked-list-empty 4) == 0 then "yes" else "no"))
   print-line-uni "-- reached the end, so this arm resolved both --"
  end
